\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When the Lord of Love was here,
\par Happy hearts to Him were dear,
\par Though His heart was sad;
\par Worn and lonely for our sake,
\par Yet He turned aside to made 
\par All the weary glad.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Meek and lowly were His ways;
\par From His loving, grew His praise,
\par From His giving, prayer;
\par All the outcasts thronged to hear;
\par All the sorrowful drew near
\par To enjoy His care.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When He walked the fields, He drew 
\par From the flowers, and birds, and dew,
\par Parables of God;
\par For within His heart of love
\par All the soul of man did move,
\par God had His abode.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Fill us, Lord, with Thy desire
\par All the sinful to inspire
\par With the Father's life;
\par Free us from the cares that press
\par On the heart of worldliness,
\par From the fret and strife.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lord, be ours Thy power to keep,
\par In the very heart of grief
\par And in trial, love;
\par In our meekness to be wise,
\par And through sorrow to arise
\par To our God above.
\par                      Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

